    "correctAnswerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Major U.S. commercial banks like JPMorgan Chase dominate USD-related FX spot trading as primary market makers, accounting for approximately 40% of global USD FX volume. Institutional investors and multinational corporations are participants but not primary market makers—banks provide continuous bid-ask quotes and liquidity.\n美国主要商业银行（如摩根大通）作为主要做市商主导美元相关外汇现货交易，约占全球美元外汇交易量的40%。机构投资者和跨国公司是市场参与者但非主要做市商——银行提供连续的买卖报价和流动性。",
    "category": "1. Macroeconomics / 宏观经济学"
