    "correctAnswerIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Earnings Per Share (EPS) measures how much profit a company generates per share: EPS = (Net Income - Preferred Dividends) / Weighted Average Diluted Shares Outstanding. Higher EPS indicates stronger profitability. For Q4 2023, Apple reported EPS of $2.18 (beating estimates of $2.10), driving the stock up 7% that day. Companies report both basic EPS (using basic shares) and diluted EPS (including options/convertibles). Diluted EPS is more conservative and widely used. EPS growth is a key valuation driver—the S&P 500's average EPS grows 6-8% annually.\nEPS（每股收益）衡量公司每股产生多少利润：EPS =（净利润 - 优先股股息）/ 加权平均稀释流通股。EPS越高表明盈利能力越强。2023年第四季度，苹果公布EPS为2.18美元（超过2.10美元的预期），推动股价当天上涨7%。公司报告基本EPS（使用基本股份）和稀释EPS（包括期权/可转换证券）。稀释EPS更保守且广泛使用。EPS增长是关键估值驱动因素——标普500的平均EPS年增长6-8%。",
    "category": "2. Stocks / 股票"
  },
