    "correctAnswerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Price-to-Book (P/B) ratio = Market Cap / Book Value (shareholders' equity). High P/B ratios (>3) occur when companies generate strong ROE (Return on Equity), indicating efficient use of assets to generate profits. Tech companies like Apple (P/B ~50, ROE ~171%) have high P/B because book value understates intangible assets like brand, patents, and software. Banks typically have low P/B (~0.8-1.2) as their assets are mostly tangible. Warren Buffett favors companies with ROE >15% and reasonable P/B. High P/B without high ROE may signal overvaluation.\n市净率（P/B）= 市值 / 账面价值（股东权益）。高P/B比率（>3）发生在公司产生强劲ROE（净资产收益率）时，表明高效使用资产创造利润。苹果等科技公司（P/B约50，ROE约171%）拥有高P/B，因为账面价值低估了品牌、专利和软件等无形资产。银行通常拥有低P/B（约0.8-1.2），因为其资产大多是有形的。巴菲特青睐ROE >15%且P/B合理的公司。高P/B但没有高ROE可能表明估值过高。",
    "category": "2. Stocks / 股票"
  },
