    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "The key distinction is that ETFs trade on exchanges throughout the day at market prices (like stocks), while mutual funds trade only once daily at NAV (Net Asset Value) after market close. For example, you can buy SPY (S&P 500 ETF) at 11:30 AM for $450.23, but if you order VFIAX (Vanguard S&P 500 mutual fund) at 11:30 AM, you'll get the NAV calculated at 4 PM close. This intraday liquidity allows ETF investors to react to news instantly, use limit orders, and employ strategies like options. However, frequent intraday trading can increase costs.\n关键区别在于ETF全天在交易所以市场价格交易（像股票），而共同基金每天只在收盘后以NAV（净资产价值）交易一次。例如，你可以在上午11:30以450.23美元买入SPY（标普500 ETF），但如果你在上午11:30下单VFIAX（先锋标普500共同基金），你会获得下午4点收盘时计算的NAV。这种日内流动性允许ETF投资者立即对新闻作出反应，使用限价订单，并采用期权等策略。然而，频繁的日内交易会增加成本。",
    "category": "3. ETF / 交易所交易基金"
  },
