    "correctAnswerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Thematic ETFs concentrate on specific investment themes or trends rather than broad market exposure. ARKK (ARK Innovation ETF), managed by Cathie Wood since 2014, focuses on disruptive innovation across sectors like genomics, fintech, and AI—holding companies like Tesla (9.8%), Coinbase, and Roku. At its peak in February 2021, ARKK reached $156/share with $28B AUM, but fell 75% by 2022 as tech valuations corrected. Unlike SPY (broad S&P 500) or GLD (single commodity), thematic ETFs carry high concentration risk but offer targeted exposure to emerging trends.\n主题ETF专注于特定投资主题或趋势，而非广泛市场敞口。ARKK（ARK创新ETF）由Cathie Wood自2014年管理，聚焦于基因组学、金融科技和AI等颠覆性创新——持有特斯拉（9.8%）、Coinbase和Roku等公司。2021年2月ARKK达到峰值156美元/股，管理资产280亿美元，但随着科技股估值修正，2022年下跌75%。与SPY（广泛的标普500）或GLD（单一大宗商品）不同，主题ETF具有高集中度风险，但提供对新兴趋势的精准敞口。",
    "category": "3. ETF / 交易所交易基金"
  },
