    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Leveraged ETFs use derivatives (swaps, futures) and daily rebalancing to amplify returns—e.g., TQQQ seeks 3× daily Nasdaq-100 performance. However, this causes volatility decay in choppy markets: if an index drops 10% then rises 10%, you are down 1%, but a 3× leveraged ETF compounds losses to -9%. For example, in March 2020, TQQQ fell 72% in 30 days despite Nasdaq declining only 30%. Studies show holding leveraged ETFs beyond 1-3 days erodes returns by 15-40% annually in volatile periods. They are designed for intraday tactical trades, not long-term holding.\n杠杆ETF使用衍生品（掉期、期货）和每日再平衡来放大回报——例如TQQQ寻求纳斯达克100指数3倍日回报。然而，这在波动市场中导致波动率损耗：如果指数下跌10%再上涨10%，你净亏1%，但3倍杠杆ETF复合损失达-9%。例如，2020年3月TQQQ在30天内下跌72%，而纳斯达克仅下跌30%。研究显示，持有杠杆ETF超过1-3天在波动期会侵蚀15-40%的年回报。它们专为日内战术交易设计，不适合长期持有。",
    "category": "3. ETF / 交易所交易基金"
