    "correctAnswerIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "To invest in ETFs, you must first open a brokerage account with platforms like Fidelity, Charles Schwab, Interactive Brokers, or Robinhood. The process typically takes 10-15 minutes online: provide SSN, employment info, and link a bank account. Most brokers now offer commission-free ETF trading—Schwab eliminated commissions in 2019, saving investors an average of $7-10 per trade. After account approval (1-3 days), you can search for ETFs by ticker (e.g., SPY, QQQ), place market or limit orders, and monitor holdings via mobile apps. Selecting a thematic ETF comes after account setup, and monitoring performance is an ongoing task, not the first step.\n要投资ETF，你必须首先在富达、嘉信理财、盈透证券或Robinhood等平台开设经纪账户。在线流程通常需10-15分钟：提供社会安全号、就业信息并链接银行账户。大多数经纪商现在提供免佣金ETF交易——嘉信在2019年取消佣金，为投资者平均节省每笔交易7-10美元。账户批准后（1-3天），你可以按代码（如SPY、QQQ）搜索ETF，下市价或限价单，并通过移动应用监控持仓。选择主题ETF在账户设置之后，监控表现是持续任务而非第一步。",
