    "id": 25,
    "content": "Why are ETFs generally more tax-efficient than mutual funds?\n为什么ETF通常比共同基金更具税务效率？",
    "options": [
      "In-kind redemptions\n实物赎回",
      "Lower expense ratios\n较低的费用率",
      "Higher liquidity\n较高的流动性"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "ETFs use in-kind redemption mechanisms, exchanging shares for underlying securities rather than cash, which avoids triggering taxable capital gains. When mutual funds redeem shares, they must sell holdings and realize gains (distributed to all shareholders). For example, actively managed mutual funds distribute average capital gains of 1.5-3% annually, while ETFs average <0.5%. This tax efficiency saved SPY investors an estimated 0.8-1.2% annually over 20 years compared to similar mutual funds. Vanguard study shows ETFs defer taxes until you sell, while mutual funds force annual tax events. Lower expense ratios (0.03% for SPY vs 0.5%+ for mutual funds) help returns, but in-kind redemptions are the key tax advantage.\nETF使用实物赎回机制，将份额交换为基础证券而非现金，避免触发应税资本收益。当共同基金赎回份额时，必须出售持仓并实现收益（分配给所有股东）。例如，主动管理的共同基金平均每年分配1.5-3%的资本收益，而ETF平均<0.5%。这种税务效率使SPY投资者在20年内相比类似共同基金每年节省约0.8-1.2%。先锋的研究显示ETF推迟税收直到你卖出，而共同基金强制年度税收事件。较低的费用率（SPY 0.03% vs 共同基金0.5%+）有助于回报，但实物赎回是关键税务优势。",
    "category": "3. ETF / 交易所交易基金"
  },
