    "id": 26,
    "content": "Which investment horizon is most suitable for leveraged ETFs?\n哪个投资期限最适合杠杆ETF？",
    "options": [
      "Short-term trading (days to weeks)\n短期交易（数天至数周）",
      "Long-term holding (years)\n长期持有（数年）",
      "No time restriction\n无时间限制"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Leveraged ETFs are explicitly designed for short-term tactical trading (days to weeks), not long-term holding (years). Due to daily rebalancing and compounding effects, they deviate significantly from their target multiple over extended periods. For instance, TQQQ (3× Nasdaq-100) returned +175% in 2020 when Nasdaq gained 44%—underperforming its 132% theoretical target due to volatility decay. ProShares' prospectus warns: \"Not suitable for holding longer than a single day.\" In volatile 2022, SQQQ (3× inverse Nasdaq) lost 80% despite Nasdaq falling 33%. Leveraged ETFs work best for experienced traders making directional bets over 1-5 days, with tight stop-losses to manage risk.\n杠杆ETF明确设计用于短期战术交易（数天至数周），不适合长期持有（数年）。由于每日再平衡和复利效应，它们在较长时间内会显著偏离目标倍数。例如，TQQQ（3倍纳斯达克100）在2020年纳斯达克上涨44%时回报+175%——低于132%的理论目标，因波动率损耗。ProShares招股说明书警告："不适合持有超过一天。"在波动的2022年，SQQQ（3倍反向纳斯达克）损失80%，尽管纳斯达克下跌33%。杠杆ETF最适合有经验的交易者在1-5天内进行方向性押注，并设置严格止损以管理风险。",
    "category": "3. ETF / 交易所交易基金"
  },
  {
    "id": 27,
    "content": "In which market environment does volatility decay most severely erode leveraged ETF value?\n在哪种市场环境下波动率损耗最严重？",
    "options": [
      "Highly volatile (ups and downs) markets\n高度波动（起伏）的市场",
      "Steadily rising markets\n稳步上涨的市场",
      "Steadily falling markets\n稳步下跌的市场"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Volatility decay (also called \"beta slippage\") erodes leveraged ETF value most severely in highly volatile, choppy markets with frequent reversals. The mathematical reason: daily rebalancing compounds losses asymmetrically. If an index oscillates +5%/-5% for 10 days, it ends flat, but a 3× leveraged ETF loses ~7.5% due to daily reset. During March 2020's extreme volatility (VIX >80), TQQQ lost 72% despite Nasdaq's 30% drop—2.4× decay. In steadily trending markets (up or down), leveraged ETFs track closer to their target multiple. For example, during Nasdaq's smooth 2023 rally (+43%), TQQQ gained 115% (2.7× multiple, closer to 3×). This is why leveraged products suit short-term directional bets in stable trends, not range-bound chop.\n波动率损耗（也称"贝塔滑点"）在高度波动、频繁反转的市场中最严重地侵蚀杠杆ETF价值。数学原因：每日再平衡不对称地复合损失。如果指数振荡+5%/-5%持续10天，最终持平，但3倍杠杆ETF会损失约7.5%，因为每日重置。在2020年3月极端波动期（VIX>80），TQQQ损失72%，而纳斯达克仅下跌30%——2.4倍衰减。在稳步趋势市场（上涨或下跌）中，杠杆ETF更接近目标倍数。例如，在纳斯达克2023年平稳上涨（+43%）期间，TQQQ上涨115%（2.7倍，接近3倍）。这就是为什么杠杆产品适合稳定趋势中的短期方向性押注，而非区间震荡。",
    "category": "3. ETF / 交易所交易基金"
  },
  {
    "id": 28,
    "content": "What is the payoff for a long call at expiration if S_T > X?\n如果标的价格S_T>行权价X，看涨期权买方到期收益是多少？",
    "options": [
      "Max(0, X - S_T)\nMax(0, X - S_T)",
      "Max(0, S_T - X)\nMax(0, S_T - X)",
      "Premium paid\n已付权利金"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "At expiration, a long call option's payoff is max(0, S_T - X), where S_T is the stock price and X is the strike price. If the stock closes above the strike (S_T > X), you profit by the difference minus the premium paid. For example, if you buy an Apple $180 call for $5 and Apple closes at $190, your payoff is $10 per share ($190-$180), and net profit is $5 ($10-$5 premium). If Apple closes at or below $180, the option expires worthless and you lose the $5 premium. This asymmetric payoff structure—unlimited upside, limited downside (premium)—is why calls are popular for bullish bets. The breakeven point is Strike + Premium ($185 in this example).\n到期时，看涨期权买方的收益是max(0, S_T - X)，其中S_T是股价，X是行权价。如果股票收盘高于行权价（S_T > X），你获利差额减去已付权利金。例如，如果你以5美元买入苹果180美元看涨期权，苹果收于190美元，你的收益是每股10美元（190-180），净利润是5美元（10-5权利金）。如果苹果收于或低于180美元，期权过期作废，你损失5美元权利金。这种不对称收益结构——无限上行，有限下行（权利金）——是看涨期权受欢迎的原因。盈亏平衡点是行权价+权利金（本例中为185美元）。",
    "category": "4. Options / 期权"
  },
  {
    "id": 29,
    "content": "For a short put seller, what is the maximum risk?\n对于看跌期权卖方，最大风险是多少？",
    "options": [
      "Unlimited\n无限",
      "Limited to premium received\n限于收到的权利金",
      "Limited to X - premium (down to zero)\n限于X-权利金（直至归零）"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "When you sell (write) a put option, you're obligated to buy the stock at strike price X if the buyer exercises. Maximum risk occurs if the stock plummets to zero—you must buy worthless shares at X, losing X minus the premium received. For example, selling a Tesla $200 put for $8 premium means: if Tesla drops to $50, you lose $142 per share ($200-$50-$8). If Tesla goes to $0, you lose $192 ($200-$8). Unlike short calls (unlimited risk as stock can rise infinitely), short puts have limited risk because stocks can't fall below zero. However, \"limited\" doesn't mean \"small\"—a $200 put has $192 downside per contract (100 shares = $19,200 risk). This is why put sellers should reserve capital to cover assignment.\n当你卖出（承做）看跌期权时，如果买方行权，你有义务以行权价X买入股票。最大风险发生在股票跌至零时——你必须以X买入无价值股票，损失X减去收到的权利金。例如，以8美元权利金卖出特斯拉200美元看跌期权意味着：如果特斯拉跌至50美元，你每股损失142美元（200-50-8）。如果特斯拉归零，你损失192美元（200-8）。与看涨期权卖方不同（无限风险，因股票可无限上涨），看跌期权卖方风险有限，因为股票不能跌破零。然而，"有限"并不意味着"小"——200美元看跌期权每份合约有192美元下行风险（100股=19,200美元风险）。这就是为什么看跌期权卖方应预留资金以应对被指派。",
    "category": "4. Options / 期权"
  },
  {
    "id": 30,
    "content": "If a call has positive intrinsic value, it is classified as:\n如果看涨期权具有正的内在价值，它被分类为？",
    "options": [
      "Out-of-the-Money (OTM)\n虚值 (OTM)",
      "At-the-Money (ATM)\n平值 (ATM)",
      "In-the-Money (ITM)\n实值 (ITM)"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "A call option is In-The-Money (ITM) when the current stock price S exceeds the strike price X, giving it positive intrinsic value = S - X. For example, if Apple trades at $190 and you hold a $180 call, it's $10 ITM with $10 intrinsic value (plus any time value). ITM options have higher premiums due to intrinsic value and greater probability of profitable exercise—delta typically 0.6-0.9 (moves $60-$90 per $100 stock move). At-The-Money (ATM) options have S ≈ X with zero intrinsic value and maximum time value. Out-of-The-Money (OTM) options have S < X (for calls), zero intrinsic value, and trade purely on time value—cheaper but lower probability of profit. Deep ITM calls (delta ~0.9) behave like stock ownership.\n当当前股价S超过行权价X时，看涨期权为实值（ITM），具有正内在价值 = S - X。例如，如果苹果交易价190美元，你持有180美元看涨期权，它是10美元实值，有10美元内在价值（加上任何时间价值）。ITM期权因内在价值和更高盈利行权概率而溢价更高——delta通常为0.6-0.9（股票每涨100美元期权涨60-90美元）。平值（ATM）期权S ≈ X，无内在价值但时间价值最大。虚值（OTM）期权S < X（看涨期权），无内在价值，纯粹基于时间价值交易——更便宜但盈利概率更低。深度实值看涨期权（delta约0.9）表现类似股票所有权。",
    "category": "4. Options / 期权"
  },
  {
    "id": 31,
    "content": "What does option time value represent?\n期权时间价值代表什么？",
    "options": [
      "The immediate exercise value\n立即行权价值",
      "Extra premium for potential favorable moves before expiration\n为到期前潜在有利变动支付的额外权利金",
      "The risk-free interest rate\n无风险利率"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Time value represents the extra premium above intrinsic value, reflecting the probability that the option will become more profitable before expiration. Formula: Time Value = Option Premium - Intrinsic Value. For example, if Tesla trades at $250 and a $240 call costs $18, intrinsic value is $10 ($250-$240) and time value is $8 ($18-$10). Time value peaks at At-The-Money (ATM) options and decays exponentially as expiration approaches (\"theta decay\"). A 30-day ATM option might lose 50% of its time value in the final 10 days. Longer-dated options have higher time value—a 1-year call may cost $40 vs $15 for a 1-month call with same strike. This is why sellers of near-expiration options profit from time decay, while buyers need fast price movement to overcome it.\n时间价值代表超出内在价值的额外权利金，反映期权在到期前变得更有利可图的概率。公式：时间价值 = 期权权利金 - 内在价值。例如，如果特斯拉交易价250美元，240美元看涨期权成本18美元，内在价值为10美元（250-240），时间价值为8美元（18-10）。时间价值在平值（ATM）期权达到峰值，并随着到期日临近呈指数衰减（"theta衰减"）。30天ATM期权可能在最后10天损失50%的时间价值。期限更长的期权有更高时间价值——1年期看涨期权可能成本40美元，而相同行权价的1个月期权为15美元。这就是为什么临近到期期权的卖方从时间衰减中获利，而买方需要快速价格变动来克服它。",
    "category": "4. Options / 期权"
  },
  {
    "id": 32,
    "content": "What does a call option give the buyer the right to do?\n看涨期权赋予买方什么权利？",
    "options": [
      "Sell the underlying asset\n卖出标的资产",
      "Buy the underlying asset\n买入标的资产",
      "Hold the underlying asset\n持有标的资产"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "A call option gives the buyer the contractual right—but not the obligation—to purchase the underlying asset (usually 100 shares per contract) at a predetermined strike price before or at expiration. For example, buying a Microsoft $400 call for $12 (total $1,200 for 100 shares) gives you the right to buy 100 MSFT shares at $400 anytime before expiration, regardless of market price. If MSFT rallies to $430, you can exercise and buy at $400, then sell at $430 for $18 profit per share ($1,800 net after $1,200 premium). If MSFT stays below $400, you let the option expire worthless and only lose the $1,200 premium. This limited-risk structure makes calls popular for bullish speculation and hedging.\n看涨期权赋予买方合同权利——但非义务——在到期前或到期时以预定的行权价购买标的资产（通常每份合约100股）。例如，以12美元买入微软400美元看涨期权（100股总计1,200美元）使你有权在到期前任何时候以400美元买入100股MSFT，无论市场价格如何。如果MSFT涨至430美元，你可以行权以400美元买入，然后以430美元卖出，每股获利18美元（扣除1,200美元权利金后净赚1,800美元）。如果MSFT保持在400美元以下，你让期权过期作废，只损失1,200美元权利金。这种有限风险结构使看涨期权成为看涨投机和对冲的流行工具。",
    "category": "4. Options / 期权"
  },
  {
    "id": 33,
    "content": "American options can be exercised:\n美式期权可以在何时行权？",
    "options": [
      "Only at expiration\n仅在到期时",
      "Anytime before or on expiration\n到期前或到期时的任何时间",
      "Only on specific dates\n仅在特定日期"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "American-style options can be exercised at any time before or on the expiration date, providing maximum flexibility for the holder. For example, if you own an American call on Tesla and it spikes 30% due to earnings, you can immediately exercise and capture gains without waiting for expiration. In contrast, European-style options (common in indexes like SPX) can only be exercised at expiration. Most U.S. equity options (stocks, ETFs) are American-style, while index options are often European. American options trade at slight premiums (~2-5%) over European equivalents due to early exercise flexibility. However, early exercise is rarely optimal for calls (better to sell the option to capture time value), except in rare cases like capturing dividends before ex-date.\n美式期权可以在到期日前或到期日的任何时间行权，为持有人提供最大灵活性。例如，如果你持有特斯拉美式看涨期权且它因财报飙升30%，你可以立即行权并锁定收益，无需等待到期。相比之下，欧式期权（如SPX等指数期权常见）只能在到期时行权。大多数美国股票期权（股票、ETF）是美式，而指数期权通常是欧式。由于提前行权灵活性，美式期权交易价比等价欧式期权高约2-5%。然而，提前行权对看涨期权很少是最优的（最好卖出期权以捕获时间价值），除非在罕见情况下如在除息日前捕获股息。",
    "category": "4. Options / 期权"
  },
  {
    "id": 34,
    "content": "For a long call, the breakeven point is:\n看涨期权买方的盈亏平衡点是？",
    "options": [
      "Strike - Premium\n行权价 - 权利金",
      "Strike + Premium\n行权价 + 权利金",
      "Strike only\n仅行权价"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "For a long call position, the breakeven point at expiration is Strike Price + Premium Paid. This is the stock price level where your total profit equals zero (ignoring commissions). For example, if you buy an Amazon $180 call for $7, your breakeven is $187. If Amazon closes at $187, the call's intrinsic value is $7 ($187-$180), exactly offsetting your $7 cost. Below $187, you lose money (max loss = $7 premium). Above $187, every dollar of stock gain becomes profit—e.g., at $200, you profit $13 per share ($200-$187). This formula helps traders quickly assess risk/reward: if you expect the stock to reach $195, the potential $8 profit ($195-$187) must justify the $7 downside risk.\n对于看涨期权多头头寸，到期时的盈亏平衡点是行权价+已付权利金。这是你的总利润等于零的股价水平（忽略佣金）。例如，如果你以7美元买入亚马逊180美元看涨期权，你的盈亏平衡点是187美元。如果亚马逊收于187美元，看涨期权的内在价值是7美元（187-180），恰好抵消你的7美元成本。低于187美元，你亏钱（最大损失=7美元权利金）。高于187美元，股票每涨一美元都成为利润——例如在200美元时，你每股获利13美元（200-187）。这个公式帮助交易者快速评估风险/回报：如果你预期股票达到195美元，8美元潜在利润（195-187）必须证明7美元下行风险是合理的。",
    "category": "4. Options / 期权"
  },
  {
    "id": 35,
    "content": "For a long put buyer, the loss is limited to:\n看跌期权买方的损失限于？",
    "options": [
      "Unlimited downside\n无限下行",
      "The premium paid\n已付权利金",
      "X - S_T\nX - S_T"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "For a long put buyer, the maximum loss is strictly limited to the premium paid, which occurs if the stock price stays above the strike at expiration, rendering the option worthless. For example, if you buy a Netflix $450 put for $15 ($1,500 per contract for 100 shares) betting on a decline, but Netflix stays at $460 or rises, the put expires Out-of-The-Money (OTM) and you lose the full $1,500. This limited-risk structure contrasts with short selling stock, where losses are theoretically unlimited if the stock rises. The maximum profit for a long put is Strike - Premium (achieved if stock drops to $0). Breakeven point = Strike - Premium. For the Netflix example: breakeven at $435 ($450-$15), max profit $43,500 if Netflix drops to $0 ($450×100 - $1,500).\n对于看跌期权买方，最大损失严格限于已付权利金，当股票价格在到期时保持在行权价之上时发生，使期权变得毫无价值。例如，如果你以15美元买入Netflix 450美元看跌期权（每份合约100股计1,500美元）押注下跌，但Netflix保持460美元或上涨，看跌期权到期为虚值（OTM），你损失全部1,500美元。这种有限风险结构与卖空股票形成对比，后者如果股票上涨损失理论上是无限的。看跌期权买方的最大利润是行权价-权利金（如果股票跌至0美元实现）。盈亏平衡点=行权价-权利金。对于Netflix例子：盈亏平衡点为435美元（450-15），如果Netflix跌至0美元最大利润为43,500美元（450×100-1,500）。",
    "category": "4. Options / 期权"
