    "id": 36,
    "content": "What is intrinsic value for a call option?\n看涨期权的内在价值是什么？",
    "options": [
      "Strike - Stock price (if positive)\n行权价 - 股价（如果为正）",
      "Stock price - Strike (if positive)\n股价 - 行权价（如果为正）",
      "Time value only\n仅时间价值"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Intrinsic value for a call option is the amount by which the stock price exceeds the strike price, calculated as max(0, S - X), where S is current stock price and X is strike price. It represents the immediate profit if you exercised the option right now. For example, if Nvidia trades at $520 and you hold a $500 call, intrinsic value is $20 ($520-$500). If the call trades at $28, the remaining $8 is time value. Options that are Out-of-The-Money (OTM) or At-The-Money (ATM) have zero intrinsic value and trade purely on time value. As expiration approaches, time value erodes and option price converges to intrinsic value. Deep In-The-Money (ITM) calls with high intrinsic value (e.g., $100 ITM) behave almost like owning the stock, with delta near 1.0.\n看涨期权的内在价值是股价超过行权价的金额，计算为max(0, S - X)，其中S是当前股价，X是行权价。它代表如果你现在行权的即时利润。例如，如果英伟达交易价520美元，你持有500美元看涨期权，内在价值为20美元（520-500）。如果看涨期权交易价28美元，剩余8美元是时间价值。虚值（OTM）或平值（ATM）期权的内在价值为零，纯粹基于时间价值交易。随着到期日临近，时间价值侵蚀，期权价格趋向内在价值。具有高内在价值的深度实值（ITM）看涨期权（例如100美元实值）几乎像拥有股票，delta接近1.0。",
