    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "A put option is In-The-Money (ITM) when the current stock price S falls below the strike price X, giving it positive intrinsic value = X - S. For example, if Tesla trades at $230 and you hold a $250 put, it's $20 ITM with $20 intrinsic value. ITM puts have higher premiums and greater probability of profitable exercise—delta typically -0.6 to -0.9 (option gains $60-$90 per $100 stock decline). At-The-Money (ATM) puts have S ≈ X with maximum time value. Out-of-The-Money (OTM) puts have S > X, zero intrinsic value, and trade on time value alone—cheaper but require significant stock declines to profit. Deep ITM puts (delta ~-0.9) behave like short stock positions. Put buyers typically want stocks to crash quickly before theta decay erodes time value.\n当当前股价S低于行权价X时，看跌期权为实值（ITM），具有正内在价值 = X - S。例如，如果特斯拉交易价230美元，你持有250美元看跌期权，它是20美元实值，有20美元内在价值。ITM看跌期权溢价更高，盈利行权概率更大——delta通常为-0.6至-0.9（股票每跌100美元期权涨60-90美元）。平值（ATM）看跌期权S ≈ X，时间价值最大。虚值（OTM）看跌期权S > X，无内在价值，仅基于时间价值交易——更便宜但需要股票大幅下跌才能获利。深度实值看跌期权（delta约-0.9）表现类似空头股票头寸。看跌期权买方通常希望股票在theta衰减侵蚀时间价值前快速暴跌。",
