  {
    "id": 40,
    "content": "What is a key difference between active and passive management?\n主动管理和被动管理的关键区别是什么？",
    "options": [
      "Active selects securities to outperform a benchmark, passive tracks an index\n主动管理选择证券以跑赢基准，被动追踪指数",
      "Passive management has higher fees\n被动管理费用更高",
      "Active management avoids all risks\n主动管理避免所有风险"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Active management involves portfolio managers conducting research and making buy/sell decisions to outperform a benchmark (e.g., S&P 500), charging higher fees (0.5-1.5% expense ratios). For example, Fidelity Contrafund (FCNTX) actively selects growth stocks aiming to beat the S&P 500. Passive management simply replicates an index through algorithms, with minimal trading and ultra-low fees (0.03-0.15%)—like Vanguard S&P 500 Index Fund (VFIAX) with 0.04% expense ratio. Studies show 85-90% of active managers underperform their benchmarks over 10-year periods after fees, driving $2+ trillion to shift from active to passive since 2010. However, active managers like Cathie Wood (ARKK) or Bill Ackman (Pershing Square) can deliver exceptional returns during specific cycles.\n主动管理涉及投资组合经理进行研究并做出买卖决策以跑赢基准（如标普500），收取较高费用（0.5-1.5%费用率）。例如，富达逆向基金（FCNTX）主动选择成长股以期击败标普500。被动管理仅通过算法复制指数，交易极少，费用超低（0.03-0.15%）——如先锋标普500指数基金（VFIAX）费用率0.04%。研究显示，扣除费用后，10年期内85-90%的主动管理者跑输其基准，推动2万亿美元自2010年以来从主动转向被动。然而，Cathie Wood（ARKK）或Bill Ackman（Pershing Square）等主动管理者在特定周期可以提供卓越回报。",
    "category": "5. Funds / 基金"
  },
  {
    "id": 41,
    "content": "Why have passive strategies grown in popularity?\n为什么被动策略越来越受欢迎？",
    "options": [
      "Due to cost efficiency and lower fees\n由于成本效益和较低的费用",
      "Because they always outperform active strategies\n因为总是跑赢主动策略",
      "They require more research\n需要更多研究"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Passive investment strategies have surged in popularity due to superior cost efficiency and consistent outperformance of most active managers. Since 2010, over $2.5 trillion has flowed from active to passive funds in the U.S. alone. The math is compelling: if the S&P 500 returns 10% annually, a passive fund with 0.04% fees nets 9.96%, while an active fund charging 1.2% nets only 8.8%—that 1.16% difference compounds to 32% more wealth over 30 years. Vanguard's founder John Bogle pioneered this model in 1976 with the first index fund. By 2023, passive funds held $13 trillion in U.S. equities vs $11 trillion for active. BlackRock's iShares and Vanguard dominate, offering rock-bottom fees and tax efficiency.\n被动投资策略因卓越的成本效益和持续跑赢大多数主动管理者而激增。自2010年以来，仅美国就有超过2.5万亿美元从主动基金流向被动基金。数学很有说服力：如果标普500年回报10%，费用0.04%的被动基金净回报9.96%，而收取1.2%的主动基金净回报仅8.8%——这1.16%的差异在30年复合成32%的财富差距。先锋创始人John Bogle于1976年用第一只指数基金开创了这一模式。到2023年，被动基金持有美国股票13万亿美元，而主动基金为11万亿美元。贝莱德的iShares和先锋占据主导地位，提供极低费用和税务效率。",
    "category": "5. Funds / 基金"
  },
