    "explanation": "Alternative asset managers specialize in non-traditional investments beyond stocks and bonds, including hedge funds (Bridgewater's $100B+ AUM using macro strategies), private equity (Blackstone, KKR buying private companies), real estate (commercial properties, REITs), commodities (oil, gold futures), and venture capital (Sequoia funding startups like Airbnb). These assets offer diversification benefits—low correlation to stock markets—but come with higher fees (2% management + 20% performance), longer lock-up periods (3-10 years for PE), and require accredited investor status ($1M+ net worth or $200K+ income). During 2022's stock crash, some hedge funds like Citadel gained 38% using multi-strategy approaches, demonstrating alternatives' value in downturns.\n另类资产管理者专注于股票和债券之外的非传统投资，包括对冲基金（桥水管理超过1000亿美元AUM，使用宏观策略）、私募股权（黑石、KKR收购私营公司）、房地产（商业地产、REITs）、大宗商品（石油、黄金期货）和风险投资（红杉资助Airbnb等初创公司）。这些资产提供分散化好处——与股市相关性低——但费用更高（2%管理费+20%业绩提成），锁定期更长（私募股权3-10年），并要求合格投资者身份（净资产100万美元以上或收入20万美元以上）。在2022年股市崩盘期间，Citadel等一些对冲基金使用多策略方法获得38%收益，展示了另类投资在低迷期的价值。",
