    "id": 43,
    "content": "What is the main feature of open-end mutual funds?\n开放式共同基金的主要特征是什么？",
    "options": [
      "Investors buy/redeem at NAV, funds can issue new shares\n投资者按NAV购买/赎回，基金可发行新份额",
      "Fixed number of shares traded on exchanges\n固定数量的份额在交易所交易",
      "No liquidity for investors\n投资者没有流动性"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Open-end mutual funds continuously issue and redeem shares at the daily calculated Net Asset Value (NAV), allowing unlimited growth as investor demand increases. For example, Vanguard Total Stock Market Fund (VTSAX) has grown from $50B to $1.5T AUM by issuing new shares to incoming investors. When you invest $10,000, the fund creates new shares and uses your cash to buy proportional holdings. When you redeem, the fund sells assets and returns NAV to you. NAV is calculated once daily at 4 PM ET market close: (Total Assets - Liabilities) / Outstanding Shares. In contrast, closed-end funds (CEFs) issue a fixed number of shares in an IPO and trade on exchanges at market prices that can differ from NAV by ±10-20%.\n开放式共同基金持续按每日计算的资产净值（NAV）发行和赎回份额，随着投资者需求增加允许无限增长。例如，先锋全股票市场基金（VTSAX）通过向新投资者发行新份额，从500亿美元AUM增长到1.5万亿美元。当你投资10,000美元时，基金创建新份额并用你的现金按比例购买持仓。当你赎回时，基金出售资产并将NAV返还给你。NAV在美东时间下午4点市场收盘时每日计算一次：（总资产-负债）/流通份额。相比之下，封闭式基金（CEF）在IPO中发行固定数量的份额，并在交易所以市场价格交易，可能与NAV相差±10-20%。",
    "category": "5. Funds / 基金"
