    "correctAnswerIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Hedge funds employ aggressive, flexible investment strategies unavailable to mutual funds, including leverage (borrowing 2-4× capital via margin), short selling (betting against overvalued stocks), derivatives (options, swaps, futures), and arbitrage (exploiting price discrepancies). For example, Bridgewater's Pure Alpha fund uses global macro strategies across currencies, bonds, and commodities with 150% gross exposure (50% net). Citadel's multi-strategy approach combines equity long-short, fixed income arbitrage, and quantitative trading, generating 38% returns in 2022 when the S&P 500 fell 18%. Hedge funds charge steep \"2 and 20\" fees (2% annual + 20% performance) and require $100K-$5M minimums with 1-3 year lock-ups. Unlike mutual funds' daily liquidity, hedge fund investors face quarterly redemption windows.\n对冲基金采用共同基金无法使用的激进、灵活投资策略，包括杠杆（通过保证金借入2-4倍资本）、卖空（押注高估股票下跌）、衍生品（期权、掉期、期货）和套利（利用价格差异）。例如，桥水的Pure Alpha基金使用跨货币、债券和大宗商品的全球宏观策略，总敞口150%（净敞口50%）。Citadel的多策略方法结合股票多空、固定收益套利和量化交易，在标普500下跌18%的2022年产生38%回报。对冲基金收取高额"2和20"费用（2%年费+20%业绩提成），要求10万-500万美元最低投资额和1-3年锁定期。与共同基金的每日流动性不同，对冲基金投资者面临季度赎回窗口。",
