    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Class A shares charge a front-end load (sales commission) deducted immediately when you purchase, typically 3-5.75% of your investment. For example, investing $10,000 in a fund with a 5% front-end load means $500 goes to the broker/advisor and only $9,500 is actually invested. However, Class A shares have lower ongoing expense ratios (0.5-1.0%) compared to Class B/C shares, making them cost-effective for long-term holders or large investments. Many funds offer breakpoints—reduced loads for investments over $50K, $100K, or $250K. For instance, American Funds Growth Fund of America (AGTHX) charges 5.75% for <$25K but drops to 3.5% for $100K+. Financial advisors often recommend Class A for buy-and-hold investors.\nA类份额收取前端费用（销售佣金），在你购买时立即扣除，通常为投资额的3-5.75%。例如，以5%前端费用投资10,000美元意味着500美元给经纪商/顾问，只有9,500美元实际投资。然而，A类份额的持续费用率（0.5-1.0%）低于B/C类份额，使其对长期持有者或大额投资具有成本效益。许多基金提供分档优惠——投资超过5万、10万或25万美元可降低费用。例如，美国基金成长型美国基金（AGTHX）对<2.5万美元收取5.75%，但对10万美元以上降至3.5%。财务顾问通常为买入持有投资者推荐A类。",
    "category": "5. Funds / 基金"
