  {
    "id": 49,
    "content": "What does a performance fee in hedge funds typically include?\n对冲基金的绩效费通常包括什么？",
    "options": [
      "20% of gains above a hurdle rate\n超过门槛率收益的20%",
      "Fixed annual fee only\n仅固定年费",
      "No fee based on profits\n没有基于利润的费用"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Hedge fund performance fees, part of the \"2 and 20\" fee structure, charge 20% of profits above a hurdle rate (often 5-8% annual return or SOFR + 2%). For example, if a fund with a 5% hurdle returns 15%, it charges 20% of the excess 10%, earning 2% in performance fees plus the 2% management fee = 4% total. Many funds include high-water mark provisions—no performance fees until prior losses are recovered. For instance, if your investment drops from $1M to $800K then rebounds to $950K, the fund earns no incentive until it exceeds $1M again. This aligns manager interests with investor returns. Renaissance Technologies' Medallion Fund famously charges 5% management + 44% performance yet delivers 66% average annual returns since 1988, making it history's most successful hedge fund.\n对冲基金绩效费是"2和20"费用结构的一部分，对超过门槛率（通常为5-8%年回报或SOFR+2%）的利润收取20%。例如，如果一个门槛率为5%的基金回报15%，它对超额10%收取20%，赚取2%的绩效费加上2%的管理费=总计4%。许多基金包括高水位线条款——在恢复之前的损失之前不收取绩效费。例如，如果你的投资从100万美元跌至80万美元然后反弹至95万美元，基金在超过100万美元之前不赚取激励费。这使管理者利益与投资者回报保持一致。文艺复兴科技的Medallion Fund以收取5%管理费+44%绩效费而闻名，但自1988年以来提供66%的平均年回报，使其成为历史上最成功的对冲基金。",
    "category": "5. Funds / 基金"
