  {
    "id": 50,
    "content": "What does price return for an index measure?\n指数的价格回报衡量什么？",
    "options": [
      "Price changes plus reinvested dividends\n价格变化加再投资股息",
      "Only changes in index level, ignoring dividends\n仅指数水平变化，忽略股息",
      "Total market capitalization\n股票总市值"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Price return measures only the change in an index's level, completely ignoring dividend income distributed by constituent companies. For example, if the S&P 500 Price Index rises from 4,500 to 4,950 over one year, price return is 10% [(4,950-4,500)/4,500]. However, this excludes the ~1.5-2% annual dividend yield S&P 500 companies pay. The headline \"S&P 500\" you see on news tickers is typically the price return version. Over long periods, this creates significant discrepancies—from 1988 to 2023, S&P 500 Price Return was ~1,200% while Total Return (including reinvested dividends) was ~3,200%, nearly triple. Price return is useful for tracking pure market sentiment but understates true investor gains.\n价格回报仅衡量指数水平的变化，完全忽略成分公司分配的股息收入。例如，如果标普500价格指数在一年内从4,500涨至4,950，价格回报为10%[(4,950-4,500)/4,500]。然而，这排除了标普500公司支付的约1.5-2%年股息收益率。你在新闻股票行情中看到的"标普500"通常是价格回报版本。长期来看，这造成显著差异——从1988年到2023年，标普500价格回报约1,200%，而总回报（包括再投资股息）约3,200%，近乎三倍。价格回报对追踪纯市场情绪有用，但低估了真实投资者收益。",
    "category": "6. Indexes / 常见指数"
  },
  {
    "id": 51,
    "content": "How is total return different from price return?\n总回报与价格回报有何不同？",
    "options": [
      "It excludes price changes\n排除价格变化",
      "It includes price changes and reinvested dividends\n包括价格变化和再投资股息",
      "It only considers stock splits\n只考虑股票拆分"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Total return includes both price appreciation and reinvested dividends/distributions, reflecting what an actual investor would earn if they reinvested all dividend income back into the index. Formula: Total Return = [(Ending Value + Dividends) / Beginning Value] - 1. For example, if the S&P 500 rises 8% in price and pays 2% in dividends, total return is approximately 10.16% (slightly higher due to compounding). Over 30 years (1993-2023), S&P 500 Total Return Index gained 1,600% vs Price Return of only 800%—the 800% gap represents reinvested dividends. Mutual funds and ETFs typically track total return indexes, while media headlines cite price return. When evaluating long-term performance, always use total return to avoid underestimating actual investor gains by 30-50%.\n总回报包括价格增值和再投资股息/分配，反映如果投资者将所有股息收入再投资回指数中实际会赚取的收益。公式：总回报=[(期末价值+股息)/期初价值]-1。例如，如果标普500价格上涨8%并支付2%股息，总回报约为10.16%（由于复利略高）。在30年间（1993-2023），标普500总回报指数上涨1,600%，而价格回报仅为800%——800%的差距代表再投资股息。共同基金和ETF通常追踪总回报指数，而媒体头条引用价格回报。评估长期表现时，始终使用总回报以避免低估实际投资者收益30-50%。",
    "category": "6. Indexes / 常见指数"
  },
  {
    "id": 52,
    "content": "In a price-weighted index, what determines a stock's influence?\n价格加权指数中什么决定股票影响力？",
    "options": [
      "Its market capitalization\n其市值",
      "Its per-share price\n其每股价格",
      "Equal weight for all stocks\n所有股票权重相等"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "In price-weighted indexes like the Dow Jones Industrial Average (DJIA), stocks with higher per-share prices have disproportionately larger influence on index movement, regardless of company size. The index is calculated as the sum of component prices divided by a divisor (currently ~0.163 for DJIA). For example, UnitedHealth Group at $500/share has 10× the impact of Intel at $50/share, even if Intel has larger market cap. A 1% move in UnitedHealth ($5) moves the Dow ~31 points, while a 1% Intel move ($0.50) contributes only ~3 points. This creates distortions—in 2020, Apple's 4-for-1 stock split reduced its Dow weight from 12% to 3% overnight despite zero economic change. Price-weighting is considered outdated; most modern indexes use market-cap weighting (S&P 500) or equal weighting.\n在道琼斯工业平均指数（DJIA）等价格加权指数中，每股价格较高的股票对指数变动的影响不成比例地更大，无论公司规模如何。指数计算为成分股价格总和除以除数（DJIA当前约0.163）。例如，每股500美元的联合健康集团的影响力是每股50美元的英特尔的10倍，即使英特尔市值更大。联合健康1%的波动（5美元）使道指移动约31点，而英特尔1%的波动（0.50美元）仅贡献约3点。这造成扭曲——2020年，苹果4拆1股票拆分使其道指权重一夜之间从12%降至3%，尽管经济上没有变化。价格加权被认为过时；大多数现代指数使用市值加权（标普500）或等权重。",
    "category": "6. Indexes / 常见指数"
  },
  {
    "id": 53,
    "content": "Which index uses market-cap weighting?\n哪个指数使用市值加权？",
    "options": [
      "Dow Jones Industrial Average\n道琼斯工业平均指数",
      "S&P 500\n标准普尔500指数",
      "S&P 500 Equal Weight Index\n标普500等权重指数"
    ],
    "correctAnswerIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "The S&P 500 uses market-capitalization weighting, where each company's influence is proportional to its total market value (stock price × shares outstanding). For example, as of 2024, Apple at $3T market cap represents ~7% of the index, while smaller constituents like Macy's at $5B represent <0.01%. This means a 1% Apple move impacts the index 600× more than a 1% Macy's move. Market-cap weighting naturally reflects economic reality—larger companies drive more market activity—and requires minimal rebalancing (stocks self-adjust as prices change). However, it creates concentration risk: the top 10 stocks (Apple, Microsoft, Amazon, Nvidia, etc.) account for 30% of S&P 500 weight. This method is far superior to price-weighting (DJIA) and underlies 90% of index funds globally.\n标普500使用市值加权，每家公司的影响力与其总市值（股价×流通股）成正比。例如，截至2024年，市值3万亿美元的苹果代表指数约7%，而市值50亿美元的梅西百货等较小成分股代表<0.01%。这意味着苹果1%的波动对指数的影响是梅西百货1%波动的600倍。市值加权自然反映经济现实——较大公司驱动更多市场活动——并且需要最少的再平衡（股票随价格变化自动调整）。然而，它造成集中风险：前10只股票（苹果、微软、亚马逊、英伟达等）占标普500权重的30%。这种方法远优于价格加权（道指），并支撑全球90%的指数基金。",
    "category": "6. Indexes / 常见指数"
  },
  {
    "id": 54,
    "content": "What does the Russell 2000 index focus on?\n罗素2000指数关注什么？",
